Subject: [PATCH] Allow generating the AirPlay 2 plist data without host plistutil/xxd

Upstream requires the host programs plistutil and xxd to convert
plists/get_info_response.xml into a C byte array. Neither is available
in a cross-compilation environment such as the OpenWrt build system,
and the libplist package in the OpenWrt feeds has no host build.

Use python3 (which the OpenWrt build system requires anyway) to build
the binary property list, and keep plistutil+xxd as a fallback.
configure.ac now accepts either of the two paths.

A parse error is fatal on purpose. 5.6.2 shipped a get_info_response.xml
with a stray </dict> -- libplist tolerated it, python did not, and the
old version of this patch "fixed" it by deleting closing tags until the
document parsed. Upstream 5.6.3 corrected the XML itself, so the guessing
is gone: a malformed plist now breaks the build instead of producing a
plausible-looking but wrong byte array that only shows up as an AirPlay 2
client refusing to start a session.

---
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -452,10 +452,22 @@ AC_ARG_WITH(airplay-2, [AS_HELP_STRING([--with-airplay-2],[Build for AirPlay 2])
 if test "x$with_airplay_2" = "xyes" ; then
   using_ffmpeg=true
   AC_DEFINE([CONFIG_AIRPLAY_2], 1, [Build for AirPlay 2])
-  AC_CHECK_PROG(PLISTUTIL_CHECK,plistutil,yes)
-  AS_IF([test x"$PLISTUTIL_CHECK" != x"yes"], [AC_MSG_ERROR([plistutil can not be found. Please install plistutil for building for AirPlay 2. Maybe it's in the apt package libplist-utils.])])
-  AC_CHECK_PROG(XXD_CHECK,xxd,yes)
-  AS_IF([test x"$XXD_CHECK" != x"yes"], [AC_MSG_ERROR([xxd can not be found. Please install xxd for building for AirPlay 2.])])
+  # Generating the AirPlay 2 property list data needs a host-side property
+  # list converter. plistutil/xxd are not available in a cross-compilation
+  # environment, so python3 -- always present in an OpenWrt build -- is used
+  # instead whenever it is available.
+  AC_CHECK_PROG([PYTHON_CHECK],[python3],[yes],[no])
+  AC_CHECK_PROG([PLISTUTIL_CHECK],[plistutil],[yes],[no])
+  AC_CHECK_PROG([XXD_CHECK],[xxd],[yes],[no])
+  AC_MSG_CHECKING([for a way to generate the AirPlay 2 property list data])
+  if test "x$PYTHON_CHECK" = "xyes" ; then
+    AC_MSG_RESULT([python3])
+  elif test "x$PLISTUTIL_CHECK" = "xyes" && test "x$XXD_CHECK" = "xyes" ; then
+    AC_MSG_RESULT([plistutil and xxd])
+  else
+    AC_MSG_RESULT([none])
+    AC_MSG_ERROR([Building for AirPlay 2 needs python3, or both plistutil and xxd, on the build host.])
+  fi
   LIBPLIST_PACKAGE=libplist
   PKG_CHECK_EXISTS(libplist-2.0, LIBPLIST_PACKAGE=libplist-2.0)
   PKG_CHECK_MODULES([libplist_2_7_0], [${LIBPLIST_PACKAGE} >= 2.7.0], [AC_DEFINE([HAVE_LIBPLIST_GE_2_7_0], 1, [libplist >= 2.7.0])],[:])
diff --git a/xml_plist_codegen.sh b/xml_plist_codegen.sh
--- a/xml_plist_codegen.sh
+++ b/xml_plist_codegen.sh
@@ -23,6 +23,31 @@ printf "// Please do not edit this file!\n" > $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
 printf "// This file was automatically generated from $INPUT_FILE_NAME.\n\n" >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
 printf "#include \"$BASE_FILENAME.h\"\n\n" >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
 printf "unsigned char ${BASE_FILENAME}_plist[] = {\n" >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
-plistutil -i $1 | xxd -i >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
+# Convert the XML property list to a binary property list and emit it as a C
+# byte array. Upstream uses `plistutil -i ... | xxd -i` here, but neither
+# plistutil nor xxd is available in a cross-compilation environment such as
+# the OpenWrt build system. python3 (required by OpenWrt anyway) is used
+# instead, falling back to the upstream pipeline if python3 is missing.
+if command -v python3 > /dev/null 2>&1 ; then
+  # Any parse error aborts the build on purpose: emitting a truncated or
+  # half-correct property list would only show up much later, as an AirPlay 2
+  # client refusing to start a session.
+  python3 - "$1" >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c <<'PLEOF' || exit 1
+import plistlib
+import sys
+
+with open(sys.argv[1], "rb") as f:
+    plist = plistlib.load(f)
+
+if not isinstance(plist, dict):
+    sys.exit("%s: expected a dictionary at the top of the property list" % sys.argv[1])
+
+blob = plistlib.dumps(plist, fmt=plistlib.FMT_BINARY)
+for i in range(0, len(blob), 12):
+    sys.stdout.write("  " + ", ".join("0x%02x" % b for b in blob[i:i + 12]) + ",\n")
+PLEOF
+else
+  plistutil -i $1 | xxd -i >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
+fi
 printf "  };\n\n" >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
 printf "size_t ${BASE_FILENAME}_plist_len = sizeof(${BASE_FILENAME}_plist);\n" >> $2/$BASE_FILENAME.c
